              'Sociologist <strong>Max Weber</strong> formulated the canonical sociological definition: <em>"Power is the probability that one actor within a social relationship will be in a position to carry out his own will despite resistance, regardless of the basis on which this probability rests."</em> Similarly, <strong>Robert Dahl</strong> formulated an operational behavioral definition: <em>"A has power over B to the extent that he can get B to do something that B would not otherwise do."</em>',
