              '• <strong>Legitimacy (The Moral Justification - The Foundation):</strong> The widespread normative belief and consensus among citizens that a political regime, ruler, or rule is morally rightful, proper, and just. Legitimacy is evaluative: it tells us why a system <em>ought to be obeyed</em>.<br/>' +
              '• <strong>Authority (The Right to Command - De Jure Legitimate Power):</strong> The institutionalized, legally recognized right to govern and issue binding directives, accompanied by a moral obligation on subordinates to comply. Authority is prescriptive: it tells us who has the <em>rightful office to command</em>.'
